#   pre-move ref    fa5f831e, built in a git worktree at /tmp and run in THESE conditions
#   commit          fa5f831e + the working tree this log was taken from

This log exists to answer one question: did folding three copies of the core into one
move a number? A consolidation that moves a number means the copies were not equivalent,
which would be a much more interesting result than the tidy-up. The committed logs were
taken on a different day with a loaded container, so they are NOT the control: the
control is the pre-move commit built and run here, minutes apart, on the same machine.

===== spot check 1: cpp, P2.2, one encode row and one decode row =====
Ratios are in-process against protobuf in the SAME binary (R4). The 'min' column is
the best of 9 rounds; absolutes do not travel between runs and are shown only to make
the point that today's machine is faster than the committed log's was.

