dec-pb-arena      1307999.8    1262014.8    0.623    0.607   -0.016
dec-native        1499832.6    1442011.6    0.708    0.691   -0.017
dec-ffi           1448159.8    1403184.0    0.677    0.676   -0.001
dec-ffi-borrow     891734.6     861015.2    0.417    0.411   -0.006

Largest ratio move: see the delta column. R4's across-build control in drift.log puts
the worst RATIO drift between two builds of the SAME source at 0.240, and the worst
absolute drift at 49.01%. Every row above is an order of magnitude inside that, and the
arms the core cannot touch (pb-arena) move by the same amount as the ones it can, which
is what says this is run-to-run and not the move.

For contrast, the same rows against the COMMITTED log (bench_a17_shared.log, taken on a
loaded container on a different day): enc ffi 0.724 there against 0.634 pre-move here.
That 0.090 is the day, not the move -- which is exactly why the worktree control exists
and why the committed log is not the comparison.

===== spot check 2: rust, P2.2, same pair of rows =====
Same method: the pre-move commit built in the worktree and run minutes apart. The rust
slice's core gained the most from the fold -- java's two transcoders, this slice's
ak_enc_count_reverse and the layout export are all new code in ITS libak_core.so -- so
it is the arm where a code-layout effect would show if there were one.

arm                    pre ns      post ns      pre     post    delta
encode-prost         582680.9     586810.5    1.000    1.000   +0.000
encode-core-native     268872.8     269583.9    0.461    0.459   -0.002
encode-core-ffi-rust     424960.2     426078.2    0.729    0.726   -0.003
decode-prost        1482022.1    1470456.8    1.000    1.000   +0.000
decode-core-native    1452079.9    1453067.8    0.980    0.988   +0.008
decode-core-ffi-rust    1583220.3    1604970.0    1.068    1.091   +0.023

Worst move 0.023, on decode core-ffi-rust, whose own round spread in the same run is
wider than that. Nothing here is outside the drift bar and nothing is outside the run's
own noise.

VERDICT on the spot check: the fold moved no number. The three copies were equivalent,
which is what the byte-identical codec.rs and the additive-only diffs already said and
what this measures rather than assumes.

