boundary: 13 checks passed, 0 failed
WARNING: the -flto positive control did NOT fire, so the check above has not been
seen failing on this build. Treat the pass as unproven.

  NOTE, and it is a change: the -flto positive control in half two no longer fires.
  It fires when a control function is SMALLER than the largest timing closure in the
  image, and the largest closure moved from 1433 B to 911 B in this build, so the
  1155 B control now sits above the line instead of below it. That is a property of
  the C++ binary's inlining, not of the core: half one's checks -- the ones that say
  the entry points are CALLED and not inlined away, including under -flto -- all pass.
  The script says so itself rather than reporting an unproven pass as a pass. Treat
  half two's result on this build as unproven until the control is made to fire again.

