===== what this work unit did NOT measure =====

  * The java slice's Java-level gates. JDK 21 is the only JDK in this container and
    build.sh needs JDK 17 and JDK 8, so arms a, b and c were not compiled and the
    Java conformance run did not happen. What was verified is that its generator is
    clean, its core builds from the shared crate, and its JNI shim links and resolves
    against it -- which is the whole of what R0 touched. The rest is its own session's.
  * The csharp slice, at all: dotnet is not installed. Its two lines changed and its
    layout probe builds; nothing was run.
  * A re-take of anything. This was a re-gate. The only numbers here are the two
    spot-check tables, and they exist to show that the fold moved nothing.
  * The RPC arm on either side, and the upb ceiling arm. Neither is touched by the
    move beyond the core's path; neither was rebuilt.
  * Whether three generators writing the same three files ever disagree in practice.
    They cannot disagree by construction (one emitter, one description) and each
    slice's --check would catch it if they did, but they are not safe to run
    CONCURRENTLY and no runner does.
  * The -flto positive control in boundary.sh half two, which did not fire on this
    build. See the note above: half two's pass is unproven on this binary.

